 "id": "hubble",
 "title": "Hubble tension",
 "statement": {
  "text": "Hubble's law, officially the Hubble–Lemaître law, is the observation in physical cosmology that galaxies are moving away from Earth at speeds proportional to their distance. Thus, the farther a galaxy is from the Earth, the faster it moves away. A galaxy's recessional velocity is typically determined by measuring its redshift, a shift in the frequency of light emitted by the galaxy.",
  "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hubble's_law"
 },
